WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:06.756
RoboFATE: Bridging Risk Anticipation and Corrective Action for Long-Horizon Manipulation.

2
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.070
Long-horizon manipulation depends on more than completing the current action.

3
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.960
A small misalignment can leave the next operation at risk.

4
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:25.404
These baseline and teacher recordings show why anticipating a recoverable state matters before the task fails.

5
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.602
RoboFATE combines two complementary components.

6
00:00:32.802 --> 00:00:37.713
A Foresight Controller learns when to intervene from causal observation history.

7
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:44.058
A Mixture of Action Experts uses the captured risk to correct the scene and continue the task.

8
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:53.448
Dual-fate episodes pair a baseline failure with a successful teacher continuation from an earlier restored state.

9
00:00:53.648 --> 00:00:57.093
The teacher operates within the original remaining budget.

10
00:00:57.293 --> 00:01:02.219
Independent baseline successes provide examples of when not to intervene.

11
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:09.140
The backbone processes camera observations, the instruction, and robot state.

12
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.303
Before takeover, the Base Action Expert executes the task.

13
00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:19.473
In parallel, the Perceiver and the Foresight Controller monitor the context for an intervention decision.

14
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.257
The Perceiver compresses the current context into a latent summary.

15
00:01:27.457 --> 00:01:33.096
A causal recurrent controller accumulates summaries from past and present observations.

16
00:01:33.296 --> 00:01:39.917
It predicts an intervention trigger and a continuous risk embedding, without access to future observations.

17
00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:49.256
At the first positive decision, the Mixture of Action Experts replaces the Base Action Expert.

18
00:01:49.456 --> 00:01:53.465
The risk embedding is captured once and held until termination.

19
00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:59.211
The Perceiver and controller stop, while fresh observations continue to condition actions.

20
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.365
In each mixture layer, the current action token and fixed risk determine routing.

21
00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:10.082
Two of eight routed experts are selected for each token.

22
00:02:10.282 --> 00:02:16.460
A separate shared expert remains active, and the weighted outputs form the feed-forward representation.

23
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.588
We evaluate seventeen selected RoboDojo tasks across five capabilities.

24
00:02:24.788 --> 00:02:32.341
RoboFATE and Base Policy plus Mix use the same pretrained checkpoint and original and dual-fate action batches.

25
00:02:32.541 --> 00:02:41.425
RoboFATE achieves thirty-four point seven six percent capability-weighted success, a gain of nine point two nine percentage points.

26
00:02:42.363 --> 00:02:47.413
The largest category gains appear in long-horizon and precision manipulation.

27
00:02:47.613 --> 00:02:53.815
Long-horizon success rises from twenty-four point six seven to forty point eight nine percent.

28
00:02:54.015 --> 00:02:59.727
The protocol uses three evaluation seeds and two thousand five hundred fifty trials per method.

29
00:03:00.655 --> 00:03:07.742
On AgiBot G2, RoboFATE is evaluated on three household tasks with fifty trials per task.

30
00:03:07.942 --> 00:03:13.926
Success rates are ninety, seventy-two, and sixty percent, averaging seventy-four percent.

31
00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:18.184
The following clips show individual task and appearance examples.

32
00:03:19.113 --> 00:03:24.855
The robot organizes objects on a tabletop, combining object handling with placement.

33
00:03:29.113 --> 00:03:34.028
A second complete recording shows another tabletop organization example.

34
00:03:39.113 --> 00:03:42.985
The robot rearranges sofa cushions in a household setting.

35
00:03:49.113 --> 00:03:54.855
Refrigerator storage requires reaching, object transport, and coordinated placement.

36
00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:03.124
The tabletop task is also evaluated under changed lighting.

37
00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:13.532
A changed background provides another visual generalization condition.
